I could not run the exact worst-case computation, so this revision is a reasoned guess, not a verified solution.

The failing states share one cause: rule 1 forces `left` whenever Pac-Man heads right and a ghost is to his right. In the 14- and 16-move states, going right gives crash probability 0.000 (and 0.278 in the 18-move state), while `left` and `down` give 0.551. Removing rule 1 lets the sensor-based `any` rules choose among the safe directions instead. I also made the fallbacks progressively looser (the fully safe filter first, then the filters that drop the `nearer` terms, then just `!wall`), so there is always some allowed non-wall direction when the stricter sets are empty.

{"rules": [{"condition": "!wall & !closer_g0 & !closer_g1 & !nearer_g0 & !nearer_g1", "action": "any"}, {"condition": "!wall & !closer_g0 & !closer_g1", "action": "any"}, {"condition": "!wall & !closer_g0", "action": "any"}, {"condition": "!wall & !closer_g1", "action": "any"}, {"condition": "!wall", "action": "any"}, {"condition": "true", "action": "right"}]}
